run;
Work.Schools has two numeric variables, and the following PROC MEANS report is produced:
Which statement completes the program and creates this report?

A fundraising DATA step maintains a running total across daily gift records:
data charity.running_total; set charity.daily_gifts; retain campaign_total 0; campaign_total + gift_amount; run;
What does the statement campaign_total + gift_amount; (the SUM statement form) do?

Two regional customer data sets are concatenated:
data combined.customers; set region_east.customers region_west.customers; run;
The log reports ERROR: Variable customer_id has been defined as both character and numeric. What causes this, and what must be done to fix it?

A company keeps separate SAS data sets for three regional sales offices, each with the same variable structure, and wants one combined data set:
data work.allregions; set work.north work.south work.east; run;
What is the result of this DATA step?

To help diagnose a data-quality issue, a programmer adds the following line inside a DATA step that processes inventory counts:
if units_on_hand < 0 then putlog "WARNING: negative units_on_hand for item=" item_id units_on_hand=;
For observations where units_on_hand is negative, what happens as a direct result of this statement?

Assume that Sasuser.One does not exist and that the following SAS program is submitted at the beginning of a new SAS session.
data sasuser.one;
x=1;
y=27;
output one;
run;
What happens when this program runs?

An annual craft fair wants its vendor report available as both a PDF and a Word-compatible document from a single run:
ods pdf file="/output/vendor_report.pdf"; ods rtf file="/output/vendor_report.rtf"; proc print data=work.vendors; run; ods pdf close; ods rtf close;
What does this sequence of ODS statements accomplish?

A logistics manager wants a roster listing every warehouse location, even ones that currently have no staff assigned, alongside any assigned staff member's name.
proc sql; select w.warehouse_id, w.city, s.staff_name from warehouses as w left join staff_assignments as s on w.warehouse_id = s.warehouse_id; quit;
What happens to a warehouse_id in warehouses that has no matching row in staff_assignments?

