A coffee shop stores each transaction in work.cuptrans, with variables orderid, item, price, baristaid, and ordertime:
proc print data=work.cuptrans; var item price ordertime; run;
What effect does the VAR statement have in this PROC PRINT step?

A print shop wants a report of only its urgent orders from a larger order queue:
proc print data=work.orders; where rushorder = 'Y'; var orderid customer duedate; run;
What does the WHERE statement do in this PROC PRINT step?

An HR DATA step computes each employee's tenure:
